From: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Refuse the fork paths without an MMU

On NOMMU the wr-xterm launcher supplies a PTY using xterm's -S option.
The ordinary child-creation path and optional subprocess features cannot
use fork; fail explicitly if one is requested rather than using vfork
inside code which modifies the parent's address space and waits for it.

Signed-off-by: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Upstream: not submitted

diff --git a/main.c b/main.c
--- a/main.c
+++ b/main.c
@@ -133,6 +133,16 @@
 #include <xtermcap.h>
 #include <xterm_io.h>
 
+#ifdef __uClinux__
+/* The launcher uses posix_spawn and -S; fork is unavailable on NOMMU. */
+pid_t
+fork(void)
+{
+    errno = ENOSYS;
+    return -1;
+}
+#endif
+
 #if OPT_WIDE_CHARS
 #include <charclass.h>
 #endif
diff --git a/xterm.h b/xterm.h
--- a/xterm.h
+++ b/xterm.h
@@ -46,6 +46,11 @@
 #undef bcopy
 #include <X11/Xos.h>
 
+#ifdef __uClinux__
+/* uClibc does not declare fork on NOMMU; main.c supplies an ENOSYS stub. */
+extern pid_t fork(void);
+#endif
+
 #ifndef HAVE_CONFIG_H
 
 #define HAVE_LIB_XAW 1
